<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phocas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">547–610 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phocas was a Byzantine emperor who seized power in 602 CE after a mutiny in which the emperor Maurice was murdered. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, who had been restored to power with Maurice's help, used the murder as a pretext for war. The resulting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-sasanian-war-of-602-628">Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628</a> CE exhausted both empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phocas.jpg" alt="Phocas" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Museum · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phocas,_British_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
